# Taylor's installed copy is local-only: any Claude session rooted there cannot push
# or sync anywhere (no-cloud.py blocks `git push`, and any write into OneDrive,
# Dropbox, Google Drive or a mapped network drive). The SOURCE is hosted privately at
# github.com/Gretabar/taylor-ea so Mike can clone and update the framework from
# there. Either way, everything below either IS a record of Taylor's working
# relationships or can reconstruct one, or is a credential -- state/, logs/ and every
# token never leave any machine, in that git history or otherwise.
#
# Three layers, this is the weakest:
#   classify-and-place.py  decides where a file may land in the first place
#   no-cloud.py            blocks `git push` from Taylor's installed copy, and any
#                          write into OneDrive, Dropbox, Google Drive or a mapped
#                          network drive
#   this file              stops any of it being staged even so

# The register, the OAuth client and token, proposals, snapshots, private notes,
# the build-machine marker. All of it.
state/

# The audit mirror and every job log.
logs/

# Drafts. Regenerated, never versioned.
output/

# Credentials, wherever they end up.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
google-client.json
google-token.json
credentials.json
token*.json
*.key
*.pem

# Databases and their write-ahead companions.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Append-only records and job locks.
*.jsonl
*.lock

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
venv/

.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Machine-local Claude Code settings (for example EA_FIXTURE_MODE for a fixture session).
.claude/settings.local.json
